trier-bridge (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release: the owner's own end-to-end test pass on Ubuntu 24.04 is
    complete; what remained was presentation, done in this release.
  * In-app file browser with drive letters as labels over real paths; Task
    Manager Performance tab with live per-disk and per-adapter graphs, one
    color per resource; branded launcher icons; navy shell with an
    adjustable accent, a zoom bar, and an About page.
  * Session-critical processes and services are protected; ping and tracert
    hold their terminal window open through a shipped helper, never a shell.
  * "Software installers (.deb)" is a Default apps choice so App Center can
    be picked once and a double-click installs from then on.
  * Version 1.0.0 also gives the package a plain filename:
    trier-bridge_1.0.0_all.deb.

 -- Doug Trier <dougtrier69@gmail.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 23:28:41 -0500

trier-bridge (0.1.0~dev1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Foundations 02 to 07: discovery, everyday pages, read-only system tools,
    durable state and journal, End task and service control through polkit,
    Bridge Terminal with PowerShell names, file operations, default apps.
  * Integrations chosen at first run: tray icon, search provider, familiar
    launchers, Files context menu, Ctrl+Shift+Esc; all reversible per user.
  * New commands trier-bridge-tray and trier-bridge-search-provider with
    manual pages. Development build.

 -- Doug Trier <dougtrier69@gmail.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 07:30:00 -0500

trier-bridge (0.1.0~dev0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Foundation 01: application shell, typed core, packaging skeleton.
    Development build; no system feature is implemented.

